# What the turn dispatch model stands for. .agents/skills/turn-dispatch says how to keep it true:
# its Coverage record maps each model action to the code below.
#
# sync: the commit whose code the model was last confirmed to describe (SLNT-1017's full run).
# Move it only as the skill's step 1 and full run say. 987a04461d is mend#1739's commit on the
# SLNT-895 feature branch rebased on main; its covered files are the ones SLNT-1017's run checked.
# 0e0b2722ca is the SLNT-1113 branch rebased on main: agent-conversation.ts gained newestItems, a
# read of each session's newest item whose turn still runs, for the inbox, and nothing else. It
# claims, binds, completes or cancels no turn, so no action models it; SLNT-895's squash changed no
# covered function. Full run at 0e0b2722ca: every row as expected.
# 764de6838d is the SLNT-1199 branch: agent-conversation.ts gained inboxTurnFacts, two grouped
# reads (whether a session has a turn queued or running, and its newest turn or request time) for
# the inbox, and nothing else. It claims, binds, completes or cancels no turn, so no action models
# it. Full run at 764de6838d: every row as expected.
# 752341b3fe is the SLNT-1211 branch: agent-conversation.ts gained firstMessages, one read of each
# session's lowest-ordinal turn Mend sent and still in its history (an unnamed session's title, and
# the namer's first prompt), and nothing else. It claims, binds, completes or cancels no turn, so no
# action models it. Full run at 752341b3fe: every row as expected.
sync 752341b3fed05aaabcc9b8a000e3a00a0500f86c

model TurnDispatch.tla
model MCTurnDispatch.tla
model check.sh

path packages/sessions/src/protocol-host.ts
path packages/db/src/repos/agent-conversation.ts
path packages/agent-protocol/src/codex.ts

# How long check.sh may run on CI's four-core runner before formal.mjs stops it and fails
# naming this model (SLNT-1065, SLNT-1081). With tlx the full bounds took 2.3 minutes on CI (run
# 44103197639) and --quick 3 seconds: about 3.4 minutes on a host 1.5 times slower, and
# budget-full is about twice that.
budget-quick 5
budget-full 8
